CORE
test.c
--nondet-volatile-write-model A:observe_A --nondet-volatile-write-model B:observe_B --mmio-weak --mmio-weak-depth 1
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
MMIO write burst exceeds the modelled reorder depth
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
--
With a depth-1 buffer the two writes to A form a burst longer than the buffer,
which the bounded model cannot represent. Rather than silently
under-approximating (and missing the reordering bug that --mmio-weak-depth 2
exposes, see test.desc), the model reports "MMIO write burst exceeds the
modelled reorder depth" and tells the user to increase the depth.
